From: Zaid <283011337+nottzaid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Frame profiler

IRONLARK_FRAME_LOG=FILE: each rendered view (main, robot cameras, range
sensors) logs the CPU and GPU time of its passes (GPU timestamp
queries, read back frames later so the log never stalls the pipeline),
and each main-view frame and physics step its clock times.
IRONLARK_FRAME_LOG_DRAWS=1 times every draw. Ironlark's
tools/frame_log.py summarizes a log.

Replaces these patches of the numbered series, with what each measured
as it landed (tools/profile_forest.py, GTX 1060 3 GB, i5-4670):
- 0042-frame-profiler: nothing is logged, and nothing costs, unless set
